{"id": "EUVD-2026-82012", "enisaUuid": "16682f09-fdc8-3227-8f27-006bf5335c64", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mt76: mt7996: do not attach hif2 WED when the main WED attach failed\n\nIf the WED attach for the primary PCIe function fails, the probe path\nstill attached wed_hif2 for the secondary function, leaving the device\nin an inconsistent half-WED configuration that crashes later. The hif2\ncall also re-enabled hwrro_mode, which the failed primary attach had\njust turned off.\n\nSkip the hif2 WED setup when the primary WED device is not active.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9d1fd637336588d8118c104a025eca1341d9ec85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76144da3c6184c7850631ad79d0600ac8bf7649a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d566387df8306257d2f703a0d99fd9896400317e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c1924332e986019c6bcddf55c843361cccac73f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90351", "GHSA-v7hx-fgg2-wjqx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "014dfd8b-73ba-32eb-b668-6f4b73c058ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83eafc9251d6d30574b629ac637c56d168fcbdd9 <9d1fd637336588d8118c104a025eca1341d9ec85"}, {"id": "01f7365e-48fe-3d90-aae7-633d53120240", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "597935a3-5e52-32d0-a83d-9a481ab2caec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "83eafc9251d6d30574b629ac637c56d168fcbdd9 <76144da3c6184c7850631ad79d0600ac8bf7649a"}, {"id": "898e7621-153b-3ec6-afb5-5d8e05b97084", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "93599840-303c-33eb-8394-81ea776c05b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "982ae6db-4